wf for OS-9/68000=================ORIG holds comp.sources.games volume 18, wf (WORDFIND), as posted.  wf.cbeside it builds the OS-9 program.What changed, and why:  wf.c    The word list, the clues and the used flags come to 74K of          static data, past the 64K the compiler reaches directly (the          assembler's "value out of range"), so under OSK they are          declared `remote'.          Four function bodies end `};'.  Microware's compiler takes the          stray `;' as a declaration with no name ("identifier missing"),          so each is `}' here.  recipe  -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand: the default libraries have no          random().Measured: with the post's words file wf fills a 15 by 15 square, hiding38 of the file's 51 words, and lists the ones it hid; with words.2,-x 10 -y 10 and a title it makes a titled 10 by 10 square of its Spanishwords.DOC/wf holds the post's README and its two word files: `words', andwords.2, whose lines carry a clue after the word for -c.Build: cc wf.c -DOSK -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand